# Dex release signing — trusted publisher keys
#
# This file is Git's `gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile`. Every line names one key
# that is allowed to sign a Dex release tag:
#
#   <principal> <key-type> <key-material>
#
# for example:
#
#   releases@heydex.ai ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# Lines that are blank or start with "#" are ignored. While this file names no
# key at all — as it does right now — Dex's release verification behaves
# exactly as it did before signing existed: releases are still checked for
# integrity, but not for who published them.
#
# The release that first lists a real key here turns publisher checking on for
# every update after it. See docs/release-signing-runbook.md for how to create
# the key, sign a release, and rotate keys later.
#
# Do not paste a PRIVATE key here. Only the public half belongs in this file,
# and this file is public.
